                <pb facs="0581" n="487" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg487"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/3011: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ramer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-01-09T16:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                                1924—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 10—9:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>5. Department’s January 5, 4 p.m. Hill informs me salary and expenses for about
                    three months of Dodds and three assistants are accepted as an obligation of the
                    High Commission.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ramer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
